From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:30:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: isolate installer PATH opt-in and fork updates

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Keep release installer PATH changes opt-in, point fork updates at the selected GitHub repository, and state fork identity in the default system prompt
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: none
X-Jcode-Patch-File: 0001-installer-and-fork-updates.patch

Patch intent:
Keep source release installation non-invasive by default while supporting
explicit persistent PATH configuration through --configure-path or
JCODE_CONFIGURE_PATH. Add a validated JCODE_UPDATE_REPO override for GitHub
release, main-channel, source-bootstrap, and development-build self-update
operations, and state in the default system prompt that this agent is a fork
based on Fardjad's patches (https://github.com/fardjad/jcode).

Why it exists:
Installing a release must not silently edit shell startup files, and fork
maintainers need release binaries and source bootstrap updates to follow their
published releases without redirecting unrelated runtime traffic or checked-out
remotes. Argument parsing, truthy environment handling, and the sole PATH
mutation gate live in a focused helper so upstream installer changes conflict
locally and visibly.

Upstream integration points:
scripts/install_release.sh sources scripts/lib/install_release_policy.sh and
delegates argument parsing and final PATH policy to it.
scripts/test_install_release_policy.sh and scripts/test_install_release_metadata.sh
cover installer behavior, and README.md documents the contract.
crates/jcode-app-core/src/update.rs owns release lookup, main checks, source
bootstrap, and prepared update installation. update_dev_guard.rs owns the
GitHub ancestry comparison. jcode-update-core::PreparedUpdate carries the
selected source repository across background installation.
crates/jcode-base/src/prompt/system_prompt.md and prompt_tests.rs own the
built-in default system prompt identity.

Update guidance:
Preserve one policy gate before any shell startup mutation. Keep no arguments
as opt-out, accept --fast and --configure-path in either order, reject unknown
options, and treat only 1, true, yes, and on case-insensitively as environment
opt-ins. Keep repository input GitHub-slug-only and validated before URL or
clone construction. Preserve configured checkout upstreams, retain the selected
repository throughout a prepared source update, and preserve the fork identity
line in system_prompt.md alongside upstream's open-source attribution.

Validation:
bash scripts/test_install_release_policy.sh
bash scripts/test_install_release_metadata.sh
cargo test -p jcode-app-core update_repository --lib
cargo test -p jcode-app-core github_comparison_uses_selected_update_repository --lib
cargo test -p jcode-app-core default_update_urls_never_target_upstream_repo --lib
cargo test -p jcode-base test_skill_prompt_integration --lib
