 </div>

+Set `JCODE_UPDATE_REPO=OWNER/REPOSITORY` to use releases and main-channel
+source updates published by a GitHub fork. Fork releases must retain jcode's
+platform asset names and optional `SHA256SUMS` asset. This affects only
+self-update traffic, not provider, telemetry, account, integration, or Git
+checkout remotes. Source checkouts continue to update from their configured
+tracking upstream.
+
 ```bash
 # macOS & Linux
 curl -fsSL https://jcode.sh/install | bash
 ```

+[Windows installation instructions](https://jcode.sh/docs#install).
+
+Source release installs do not modify shell startup files by default. Pass
+`--configure-path` to persist the launcher directory in `PATH`. Automation may
+instead set `JCODE_CONFIGURE_PATH=1`; the case-insensitive values `1`, `true`,
+`yes`, and `on` enable configuration, while an unset, empty, or any other value
+does not. Either opt-in enables configuration. `--fast` and `--configure-path`
+may be supplied in either order.
+
